{title: In Christ Alone (FJ_135_en)}
{song_number: 135}
{language: en}
{artist: Keith Getty and Stuart Townend}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]In Christ alone my hope is found, [D]He is my light, [G]my strength, [A]my song; [D]this cornerstone, [G]this solid ground, [D]firm through the fiercest drought and storm. [G]What heights of love, [A]what depths of peace when fears are stilled, [D]when strivings cease. [G]My comforter, [A]my All in All, [D]here in the love of Christ I stand.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]In Christ alone, [D]who took on flesh, [G]fullness of God in helpless babe! [A]This gift of love and righteousness, [D]scorned by the ones He came to save. [G]‘Til on that cross, [D]as Jesus died, [G]the wrath of God was satisfied. [A]For ev'ry sin on Him was laid; [D]here in the death of Christ I live.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G] There in the ground His body lay, [D]light of the world by darkness slain; [G]then bursting forth in glorious day, [A]up from the grave He rose again! [D]And as He stands in victory, [G]sin's curse has lost its grip on me; [D]for I am His and He is mine, [G]bought with the precious blood of Christ.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]No guilt in life, [D]no fear in death, [G]this is the pow'r of Christ in me; [A]from life's first cry to final breath, [D]Jesus commands my destiny. [G]No pow'r of hell, [D]no scheme of man can ever pluck me from His hand; [G]'til He returns or calls me home, [A]here in the pow'r of Christ I'll stand!
{end_of_verse}
